    "body": "I could not find those padding tokens @patrick-hovsepian , should I be able to see them here?:\n\n```javascript\n            const splitter = new TextSplitterStream();\n            const stream = tts.stream(splitter, { voice });\n            (async () => {\n                let i = 0;\n                for await (const { text, phonemes, audio } of stream) {\n                console.log({ text, phonemes });\n                const blob = audio.toBlob();\n                self.postMessage({ status: \"complete\", audio: URL.createObjectURL(blob), text });\n                }\n            })();\n\n```\n\nI kept looking and I guess the issue is here, from `kokoro.js`. Setting `truncation:true` will, well, truncate. \n\n```javascript\nfor await (const sentence of splitter) {\n      const phonemes = await phonemize(sentence, language);\n      const { input_ids } = this.tokenizer(phonemes, {\n        truncation: true,\n      });\n\n      // TODO: There may be some cases where - even with splitting - the text is too long.\n      // In that case, we should split the text into smaller chunks and process them separately.\n      // For now, we just truncate these exceptionally long chunks\n      const audio = await this.generate_from_ids(input_ids, { voice, speed });\n      yield { text: sentence, phonemes, audio };\n    }\n```\n\nIn my experiments, when truncation happens, the audio also gets corrupted. So my strategy so far has been to avoid truncation at all costs, so I pre-process the text by chunking it with my own algorithm, which yields shorter chunks. However, I still do not have a solution for the pausing problem, where a long sentence without any obvious chunking boundary like punctuation etc. is chunked in a way that produces unnatural sounding playback due to the pause.\n\nSo I guess this leaves 3 potential options left:\n1. do semantic chunking, cutting off long sentences without obvious chunking boundaries at places that will still feel natural when play back. This is a lot of work, especially in multi-language environments.\n2. Increase the 509 token limit (not sure if this is even possible)\n3. Find/implement a way to add a special token to tell the model that the next \"sentence\" is not actually a new sentence, but just a continuation of the current and thus requires no pause.\n\nAny other ideas?\n\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
