    "created_at": "2025-05-19T00:09:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-19T00:09:28Z",
    "body": "Ah, yeah, that was going to be my next suggestion, to force CPU inference and see if the issue persisted. Definitely _seems_ like a bug with the underlying implementation but hard to say. \n\nI find it interesting that the device reports Out of Memory (OOM) for a bit but then starts responding again. I'm curious if it picks up from where it left off or if it starts at some other chunk. If you set a breakpoint in your code is it hung up waiting for the stream or does the stream return and is empty if it hits OOM?\n\nI'm not too familiar with the library itself and may not be able to offer much in terms of immediate assistance but maybe a dev will notice something?",
